--Description:  In the earlier attempt the join failed because CYTOGEN does not contain column "InvNo".
--              To fix this, join CYTOGEN (clinical data) to CYTOCONVERTED (CNV segments) only on the 
--              columns they share: "RefNo" and "CaseNo".  We still keep "InvNo" from CYTOCONVERTED so we
--              can see which investigation each segment belongs to.  The query focuses on breast-cancer
--              samples (Morph = 3111, Topo = 0401) and returns the first 20 copy-number segments with
--              chromosome, gain/loss type, genomic coordinates, and cell-presence flag.
SELECT c."RefNo",
       c."CaseNo",
       g."InvNo",
       g."Chr",
       g."Type",
       g."Start",
       g."End",
       g."CellsPresent"
FROM   MITELMAN.PROD.CYTOGEN       c
JOIN   MITELMAN.PROD.CYTOCONVERTED g
       ON c."RefNo"  = g."RefNo"
      AND c."CaseNo" = g."CaseNo"
WHERE  c."Morph" = '3111'
  AND  c."Topo"  = '0401'
LIMIT 20;
```
